# Shell scripts must be LF on every platform.
#
# A CRLF checkout of a .sh file fails on Linux with a confusing
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", and the production deploy script is
# the worst possible place to discover that. Git currently normalises this by
# accident via core.autocrlf; this makes it a property of the repository.
*.sh text eol=lf
